THIRD-PARTY CODE
----------------
The dsecrat scanner has NO third-party code dependencies — it is built entirely
on the Go standard library. The optional eBPF runtime sensor (dsecrat-runtime,
built only for Linux) depends on a single library, github.com/cilium/ebpf,
licensed Apache-2.0; that license applies only to the dsecrat-runtime binary.

The secret-detection regexes were derived independently from the providers'
public token-format documentation, and the entropy formulas are standard
mathematics; no third-party detection code was copied.

BUNDLED & FETCHED DATA
----------------------
The tool embeds reference data (vulnerability advisory snapshot, compliance
control packs, malware signatures) and can optionally fetch more at runtime
(OSV, NVD, EPSS, CISA KEV). See DATA_SOURCES.md for the provenance, copyright,
and required attribution of each source.
